       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day, which is about 5 times the usual maximum for metformin. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, or 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in the US. A dose that high risks severe lactic acidosis. A single dose of 4250 mg also exceeds any standard dosing.\n\nThis may be a typo. Did you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the usual maximum.\n- **425 mg PO TID**, though that isn't a standard tablet strength.\n- **1000 mg PO BID with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 4250 mg really is intended, for example under a specific protocol, please confirm that and I'll enter it with a note documenting the confirmation."
